    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d360">

                <pb facs="0422" n="406" sameAs="frus:frus1947v08/pg406"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.3261/10–3147: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Smith</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">us urgent</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">niact</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-10-31T18:00:00+03:00">October 31, 1947—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3144. Counselor Brazilian Embassy called 1745 to give following information:</p>
                <p>Assistant Chief Protocol called him at 1730 to advise that Brazilian Ambassador
                    staff no longer confined to hotel could circulate freely and that they should
                    get in touch with Intourist (Soviet Travel Agency) to make such arrangements as
                    they wished for their departure. Embassy staff could depart in groups between
                    November 1 and November 3 by such means as they chose. They can take with them
                    all personal belongings and archives which will not be opened or examined by
                    Soviet authorities. Protocol asked passports be sent immediately Foreign Office
                    obtain necessary exit visas (this being done).</p>
                <p>Brazilian Ambassador has not decided definite arrangements for departure. Soon as
                    details formulated will be cabled urgently.<anchor n="30" xml:id="d360-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>Department pass Rio de Janeiro urgently.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Smith</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d360-f1" n="30" xml:id="d360-f1-content">
                <p>The Brazilian Ambassador and his party departed for Helsinki on November 3, and
                    the Soviet staff left Rio de Janeiro in four groups on November 1, 2, and 3.
                    (701.3261/11–347; 701.6132/11–247, 11–347, and 11–447.)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
